                "entry_id": "b6a60ac0-0177-3bdd-a58a-ac826110240b",
                "word": "négritude",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "08326b06-6c71-4544-8118-e2f65120280e",
                        "entry_id": "b6a60ac0-0177-3bdd-a58a-ac826110240b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "négritudes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed9c4004-58da-308c-8cc9-61cb872c3bb1",
                        "entry_id": "b6a60ac0-0177-3bdd-a58a-ac826110240b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Courant littéraire et politique, rassemblant des écrivains noirs francophones qui revendiquent l’identité noire et sa culture."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "835685a4-2048-415c-a45e-aa63b9eba0b1",
                                "sense_id": "ed9c4004-58da-308c-8cc9-61cb872c3bb1",
                                "text": "C’est une attitude et une méthode, encore une fois, un esprit, qui, significativement, fait moins la synthèse que la symbiose de la modernité et de la négrité. Je dis « négrité » et non négritude puisqu’il s’agit de l’esprit nègre plutôt que du vécu nègre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b251682-981d-4b15-b09c-4486491b774a",
                                "sense_id": "ed9c4004-58da-308c-8cc9-61cb872c3bb1",
                                "text": "Avec à la clé le début de son engagement censé « défendre la négritude » et mettre en garde contre « un deux poids deux mesures » dans l’indemnisation des descendants des victimes de crimes historiques."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e79ab58-b4fc-4f2a-86d2-a8f83dcf81c4",
                        "source_entry_id": "b6a60ac0-0177-3bdd-a58a-ac826110240b",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed9c4004-58da-308c-8cc9-61cb872c3bb1",
                        "target_lang_word": "negritude",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "negritude",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da507598-4844-30aa-9b9f-a4c63e4b326d",
                                        "entry_id": "43e712b2-1e78-3db7-a863-c2610da3e03a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The fact of being of black African descent, especially a conscious pride in the values, cultural identity etc. of African heritage; blackness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "252f667e-2239-42de-b90a-c1a94e5c2baa",
                                                "sense_id": "da507598-4844-30aa-9b9f-a4c63e4b326d",
                                                "text": "Negritude is not wearing turbans and fezzes, though these may be quite alluring."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7babc39d-b1d1-4e94-9fb6-d1b16a75a05e",
                                                "sense_id": "da507598-4844-30aa-9b9f-a4c63e4b326d",
                                                "text": "Long before Negritude had become a war-cry among the Black intellectuals of the Left Bank, Caribbean writers had been composing verses in French that were purely derivative, evoking the Parnassian and neo-Romantic influences of the end of the last century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f94462f-c282-4bc3-b06f-d0297ee00716",
                                                "sense_id": "da507598-4844-30aa-9b9f-a4c63e4b326d",
                                                "text": "In order to explain this morality in action of negritude, I must go back a little."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cde01a3-5141-44a2-836c-6bace8aa8577",
                                                "sense_id": "da507598-4844-30aa-9b9f-a4c63e4b326d",
                                                "text": "Another important thing about “CLR,” as he was known in our little movement, was his disdainful opposition to any Third World fetishism or half-baked negritude."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f2c399f6-df20-4faa-be14-ef5839ed1499",
                        "source_entry_id": "b6a60ac0-0177-3bdd-a58a-ac826110240b",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed9c4004-58da-308c-8cc9-61cb872c3bb1",
